\title{dr3: Doubly-Robust ATE Estimators: Three Routes to One Answer}
\description{
A transparent, teaching-oriented reference implementation of the average treatment effect (ATE) estimators reconciled in "Three Routes to One Answer": g-computation, inverse-probability weighting, AIPW / one-step, and targeted maximum likelihood (TMLE), together with their cross-fit (double machine learning, CV-TMLE) and double-cross-fit (DC-AIPW, DC-TMLE) variants. Every estimator shares one Super Learner nuisance library, so differences between them come from the combination rule and the fitting scheme (and, for split-based estimators, from the random split), not from separate implementations. The package is meant for teaching and reproducibility and is cross-checked against the established 'tmle' and 'AIPW' packages, not as a replacement for them.
